# Autobee

> **Advanced primitive reference.** For new app features start with
> `@unstoppable-stack/p2p` and `modules/p2p.mdc`. Direct engine use is for
> existing storage, app-owned file operations, custom protocols or isolated
> tests. Reuse existing owners; do not rebuild managed transport/storage.


For a new simple JSON dataset, see `modules/managed-data.mdc`. Preserve Autobee
for existing schema-based apps; managed Autobase storage is not format-compatible.

## Overview

Autobee is a **multi-writer Hyperbee**. Each peer writes to its own local
Hypercore; an `apply` function you supply merges those writes into a shared
Hyperbee view deterministically. Once peers replicate, every peer's view is
identical.

This is the recommended multi-writer layer for Unstoppable apps, and what
`reference-apps/qvac-app` uses for all replicated state.

> **Autobee is not a wrapper around Autobase.** It does not depend on it — it
> is a separate implementation built on `hyperbee2` + `hypercore@11`. Do not
> mix the two APIs. See [autobase](autobase.mdc) for the older primitive.

## Version Notes

- `autobee@1.0.10` (verified 2026-07-29). Upstream marks it **experimental and
  under heavy development — expect breaking changes.** Pin an exact version.
- Deps: `hyperbee2`, `hypercore@^11`, `autobee-encryption`, `autobee-wakeup`.
- Compatible with `corestore@^7.9` (which resolves `hypercore@^11.32`).

## Installation

```bash
npm i autobee corestore b4a
```

## Quick Start

```js
import Autobee from 'autobee'
import Corestore from 'corestore'
import b4a from 'b4a'

async function apply (nodes, view, host) {
  for (const node of nodes) {
    const op = JSON.parse(b4a.toString(node.value))

    // Writer management is an operation like any other.
    if (op.type === 'addWriter') {
      await host.addWriter(b4a.from(op.key, 'hex'))
      continue
    }

    if (op.type === 'put') {
      // hyperbee2 batch API — NOT hyperbee's view.put()
      const w = view.write()
      w.tryPut(b4a.from(op.key), b4a.from(JSON.stringify(op.value)))
      await w.flush()
    }
  }
}

const store = new Corestore('./data')
const db = new Autobee(store, null, { apply })   // null key = create new
await db.ready()

await db.append(b4a.from(JSON.stringify({ type: 'put', key: 'a', value: 1 })))

const node = await db.view.get(b4a.from('a'))    // keys are Buffers
console.log(JSON.parse(b4a.toString(node.value)))
```

## Adding a Second Writer

A new peer opens the *same* Autobee by key. It starts **read-only**
(`writable === false`) until an existing writer promotes it.

```js
const db2 = new Autobee(store2, db1.key, { apply })
await db2.ready()
console.log(db2.writable)            // false

// Replicate (Autobee has its own replicate — you do not replicate the store)
const s1 = db1.replicate(true)       // initiator
const s2 = db2.replicate(false)
s1.pipe(s2).pipe(s1)

// An existing writer appends an addWriter op naming db2's LOCAL key
await db1.append(b4a.from(JSON.stringify({
  type: 'addWriter',
  key: db2.local.key.toString('hex'),
})))

// db2 becomes writable once it applies that op
while (!db2.writable) {
  await db2.update()
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100))
}
```

> `db.local.key` is the **writer** key (what you pass to `addWriter`).
> `db.key` is the **database** key (what peers use to join). Confusing them is
> the most common Autobee mistake — promoting `db.key` silently does nothing.

## API Reference

### Constructor

`new Autobee(store, [key], [options])` — `store` is a Corestore; `key` is an
existing Autobee's key to join, or `null`/omitted to create a new one.

| Option | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `apply(nodes, view, host)` | Merge batches of new nodes into the view |
| `open(bee, db)` | Build a custom view over the raw bee; return it |
| `close(view)` | Called on close |
| `update(view, changes)` | Called after apply when the view advanced |
| `encryptionKey` | 32-byte key; encrypts writer cores and view at rest |
| `encrypted` | Set `true` when using `encryptionKey` |
| `keyPair` | Custom signing key pair for the local writer |
| `optimistic` | Allow writes before being a confirmed writer |

### Properties

| Property | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `db.key` | Database public key — share so peers can join |
| `db.discoveryKey` | Use for Hyperswarm topic discovery |
| `db.local` | The local writer Hypercore (`db.local.key` for `addWriter`) |
| `db.view` / `db.bee` | Read-only Hyperbee snapshot of the merged view |
| `db.writable` | `true` once promoted to writer |
| `db.isIndexer` | `true` if this writer is an indexer |

### Methods

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `await db.append(value \| values, [opts])` | Append to the local writer; triggers apply |
| `await db.update()` | Trigger an apply cycle (call after replication) |
| `await db.updated()` | Wait for the current apply cycle to finish |
| `await db.flush()` | Wait until all known writers are fully indexed |
| `db.replicate(isInitiator)` | Create a replication stream |
| `db.wakeup({ key, length })` | Hint that a writer core is available |
| `await db.setLocal(key, [opts])` | Rotate the local writer |
| `Autobee.isAutobee(val)` | Type check |

### The `host` object (inside `apply`)

| Call | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `host.addWriter(key, [{ isIndexer }])` | Promote a writer (default `isIndexer: true`) |
| `host.removeWriter(key)` | Remove a writer |
| `host.ackWriter(key)` | Acknowledge without changing permissions |
| `host.interrupt(reason)` | Abort this apply cycle; emits `'interrupt'` |
| `await host.createAnchor()` | Verifiable checkpoint `{ key, length }` |
| `host.genesis` | `true` before any node is processed — use to bootstrap |

Each `node` in `nodes` has `node.key` (writer public key), `node.value`
(the appended Buffer), and `node.length` (position in that writer's core).

## Composing with HyperDB

For schema'd collections and indexes instead of raw key-value, build a HyperDB
over the Autobee view inside `open`:

```js
import HyperDB from 'hyperdb'
import Spec from './spec/index.js'

const db = new Autobee(store, key, {
  // MUST be synchronous — Autobee assigns `view = open(bee)` without awaiting
  // and passes the same value into apply.
  open (bee) {
    return { db: HyperDB.bee2(bee, Spec, { autoUpdate: true }) }
  },
  apply,
})
```

`HyperDB.bee2()` is the hyperbee2 variant — required for an Autobee view.
`HyperDB.bee()` targets a plain Hypercore and `HyperDB.rocks()` targets local
RocksDB. See [hyperdb](hyperdb.mdc) and the
`p2p-hyperdb-autobee-sync` recipe.

## Gotchas

- **`open` must be synchronous.** Autobee does not await it.
- **Buffer keys.** `view.get()` / `tryPut()` take Buffers, not strings.
- **`view.write()` batches.** Use `const w = view.write(); w.tryPut(...); await
  w.flush()`. There is no `view.put()` — that is the hyperbee (v1) API.
- **`writable` is false at first.** A joining peer cannot write until promoted.
  Gate writes on `db.writable` rather than assuming.
- **`db.local.key` vs `db.key`.** See the warning above.
- **`update()` after replication.** Replication delivering data does not by
  itself advance the view; pump with `db.update()`.
- **Experimental.** Pin the version and re-read the README on upgrade.
